
  THE COLLATZ CONJECTURE IN RAPIDITY SPACE

======================================================================

  I. RAPIDITY IS HALF THE LOG
  --------------------------------------------------

  Cayley address: x_n = (n-1)/(n+1) = Q^{-1}(n)
  Rapidity: rho(n) = arctanh(x_n) = (1/2)*ln(n)

  Proof: arctanh((n-1)/(n+1)) = (1/2)*ln((1+(n-1)/(n+1))/(1-(n-1)/(n+1)))
       = (1/2)*ln((2n/(n+1)) / (2/(n+1)))
       = (1/2)*ln(n)

  n=   2: x_n = 0.333333, rho = 0.346574, ln(n)/2 = 0.346574, match: True
  n=   3: x_n = 0.500000, rho = 0.549306, ln(n)/2 = 0.549306, match: True
  n=   7: x_n = 0.750000, rho = 0.972955, ln(n)/2 = 0.972955, match: True
  n=  42: x_n = 0.953488, rho = 1.868835, ln(n)/2 = 1.868835, match: True
  n= 100: x_n = 0.980198, rho = 2.302585, ln(n)/2 = 2.302585, match: True

  II. COLLATZ IN RAPIDITY SPACE
  --------------------------------------------------

  The rapidity changes:
  Even step n -> n/2: rho -> rho - ln(2)/2 = rho - 0.346574
  Odd step n -> 3n+1: rho -> (1/2)*ln(3n+1)
    For large n: ~ rho + ln(3)/2 = rho + 0.549306
    Correction: (1/2)*ln(3n+1) = (1/2)*ln(3) + (1/2)*ln(n+1/3)
              = (1/2)*ln(3) + (1/2)*ln(n) + (1/2)*ln(1+1/(3n))
              ~ rho + 0.549306 + O(1/n)

  After an odd step, the result 3n+1 is always EVEN.
  So an odd step is ALWAYS followed by at least one even step.
  Combined 'odd + k halvings': rho -> rho + ln(3)/2 - k*ln(2)/2
  = rho + (ln(3) - k*ln(2))/2

  THE 2-ADIC TREE OF COLLATZ:

  v_2(3n+1) depends on n mod 2^k:
    n = 3 mod 4: v_2(3n+1) = 1
    n = 1 mod 8: v_2(3n+1) = 2
    n = 13 mod 16: v_2(3n+1) = 3
    n = 5 mod 32: v_2(3n+1) = 4
    n = 53 mod 64: v_2(3n+1) = 5
    n = 21 mod 128: v_2(3n+1) = 6

