  IV. THE EVEN/ODD RATIO AND ln(3)/ln(2)
  --------------------------------------------------

  For rapidity to decrease to 0 (reaching n=1):
  Need: odd_steps * ln(3)/2 - even_steps * ln(2)/2 < -rho_0
  => even/odd > ln(3)/ln(2) = 1.584963
  This is the CRITICAL RATIO.

  ln(3)/ln(2) = 1.5849625007
  Continued fraction: [1; 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 1, 5, 2, 23, 2, ...]
  Convergents: 1, 2, 3/2, 8/5, 19/12, 65/41, 84/53, ...

  Even/Odd ratio for first N steps (starting from n=27):
    After   20 steps: E/O = 1.222222 (target: 1.584963, diff: -0.362740)
    After   40 steps: E/O = 1.352941 (target: 1.584963, diff: -0.232021)
    After   60 steps: E/O = 1.400000 (target: 1.584963, diff: -0.184963)
    After   80 steps: E/O = 1.424242 (target: 1.584963, diff: -0.160720)
    After  100 steps: E/O = 1.564103 (target: 1.584963, diff: -0.020860)

  Large-scale E/O ratios:
  Over all odd n in [3, 10000]: E/O = 1.97841342
  ln(3)/ln(2) = 1.58496250
  Difference: +0.39345092

