    v_2 = 1:  25000/50000 = 0.500000  (expected: 0.500000)  drift = +0.202733
    v_2 = 2:  12500/50000 = 0.250000  (expected: 0.250000)  drift = -0.143841
    v_2 = 3:   6250/50000 = 0.125000  (expected: 0.125000)  drift = -0.490415
    v_2 = 4:   3125/50000 = 0.062500  (expected: 0.062500)  drift = -0.836988
    v_2 = 5:   1562/50000 = 0.031240  (expected: 0.031250)  drift = -1.183562
    v_2 = 6:    782/50000 = 0.015640  (expected: 0.015625)  drift = -1.530135
    v_2 = 7:    390/50000 = 0.007800  (expected: 0.007812)  drift = -1.876709
    v_2 = 8:    196/50000 = 0.003920  (expected: 0.003906)  drift = -2.223283
    v_2 = 9:     97/50000 = 0.001940  (expected: 0.001953)  drift = -2.569856
    v_2 = 10:     49/50000 = 0.000980  (expected: 0.000977)  drift = -2.916430
    v_2 = 11:     24/50000 = 0.000480  (expected: 0.000488)  drift = -3.263003
    v_2 = 12:     13/50000 = 0.000260  (expected: 0.000244)  drift = -3.609577
    v_2 = 13:      6/50000 = 0.000120  (expected: 0.000122)  drift = -3.956151
    v_2 = 14:      3/50000 = 0.000060  (expected: 0.000061)  drift = -4.302724
    v_2 = 15:      1/50000 = 0.000020  (expected: 0.000031)  drift = -4.649298
    v_2 = 16:      1/50000 = 0.000020  (expected: 0.000015)  drift = -4.995871
    v_2 = 18:      1/50000 = 0.000020  (expected: 0.000004)  drift = -5.689018

  Expected drift per odd step: -0.14385490
  Theoretical: sum_{k=1}^inf (1/2^k) * (ln(3) - k*ln(2))/2
  = (ln(3)/2) * sum(1/2^k) - (ln(2)/2) * sum(k/2^k)
  = (ln(3)/2) * 1 - (ln(2)/2) * 2 = ln(3)/2 - ln(2)
  = -0.14384104

  Average drift per odd step = ln(3)/2 - ln(2) = (ln(3) - 2*ln(2))/2
  = ln(3/4)/2 = -0.14384104
  This is NEGATIVE: orbits drift DOWNWARD in rapidity on average.

